  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset titled \"Genome - Abeoforma whisleri,\" accessible on Figshare, has been cited once since its publication in 2017, indicating an early signal of scholarly uptake. This dataset has also been reused in two distinct pieces of research, showcasing its contribution to ongoing scholarly discussions.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published in 2017, the \"Genome - Abeoforma whisleri\" dataset provides valuable insights into the genetic and genomic features of this organism. Despite being published under the auspices of the Multicellgenome Lab, the authorship remains unspecified, which is not uncommon in collaborative research environments. The dataset is classified under open access and has garnered a single citation as of 2025, reflecting its nascent integration into the academic discourse.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset has been referenced in a journal article published in eLife, which discusses G-protein-coupled receptor diversity and evolution among metazoan relatives. This citation not only underscores the dataset's relevance to the field of evolutionary biology but also highlights its role in enriching the understanding of complex biological mechanisms. The presence of a notable institution, such as the University of California, Berkeley, among the top cited institutions signifies a level of recognition within academic circles.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Moreover, the dataset has been reused by researchers to support further investigations, indicating its utility beyond initial publication. Two reuse instances were noted, one in a related article and another in biomedical literature mentioned in Europe PMC. Such reuse is pivotal for advancing scientific knowledge and fostering collaborative exploration in genetics and computational biology.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, while the dataset's impact may appear limited at this time, its foundational role in subsequent research and the potential for future citations reflect its importance within the broader context of genomic studies. As the field evolves, the \"Genome - Abeoforma whisleri\" dataset may continue to serve as a critical resource for scholars navigating the complexities of biological systems.</p>",
